-- title:
--   Regular differentials of the level N function field as F(τ) dτ
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and let $A_N =$ [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) be the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of the algebra of functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by `jAnalytic` together with all Fricke functions `fricke N v` for $0 \neq v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$. Let $K$ be a field which is simultaneously a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an $A_N$-algebra, compatibly, and which is a fraction field of $A_N$. Write $\Omega_{\mathrm{reg}} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials ℂ K`](def/AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials.html#L26) for the $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of $\Omega_{K/\mathbb{C}}$ of those $\omega$ such that for every place $v$ of $K/\mathbb{C}$ — that is, every valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from $K$, and a principal ideal ring — there is $f$ in that valuation subring with $\omega = f \cdot d(t_v)$, $t_v$ a uniformiser of $v$. Two assertions are made. First, every $\omega \in \Omega_{\mathrm{reg}}$ has the shape $\omega = (a/b)\cdot d(c/e)$ for functions $a,b,c,e : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ lying in $A_N$ with $b \neq 0$ and $e \neq 0$, where $a,b,c,e$ are mapped into $K$ by the structure map and $d$ is the universal derivation of $K$ over $\mathbb{C}$. Second, there is an injective $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $\Psi : \Omega_{\mathrm{reg}} \to (\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C})$ such that each $\Psi\omega$ is holomorphic on $\mathbb{H}$, and such that for every $\omega$ and every presentation $\omega = (a/b)\cdot d(c/e)$ as above (with $a,b,c,e \in A_N$, $b,e \neq 0$) one has, for all $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$, $$\Psi\omega(\tau)\, b(\tau)\, e(\tau)^2 = a(\tau)\bigl(e(\tau)\, c'(\tau) - c(\tau)\, e'(\tau)\bigr),$$ the derivatives being complex derivatives of $c$ and $e$ transported to $\mathbb{C}$ along `UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`.
--
--   This is the analytic half of the classical identification of the differentials of the first kind on the modular curve of level $N$ with holomorphic differentials $F(\tau)\,d\tau$ on the upper half plane: a regular differential of the function field $K$ is determined by, and determines, a holomorphic function $F$ on $\mathbb{H}$ through $\omega = F(\tau)\,d\tau$, the correspondence being recorded by the displayed cross-multiplied identity so as to avoid dividing by the zeros of $b$ and $e$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective), where the image of $\Psi$ is matched with weight $2$ cusp forms of level $N$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_mdifferentiable.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped Manifold

theorem ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_mdifferentiable
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N]
    (K : Type*) [Field K] [Algebra ℂ K] [Algebra (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K]
    [IsScalarTower ℂ (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K]
    [IsFractionRing (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K] :
    (∀ ω ∈ AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials ℂ K,
      ∃ (a b c e : UpperHalfPlane → ℂ) (ha : a ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N)
        (hb : b ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) (hc : c ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N)
        (he : e ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N), b ≠ 0 ∧ e ≠ 0 ∧
        ω = (algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨a, ha⟩ /
              algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨b, hb⟩) •
            KaehlerDifferential.D ℂ K (algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨c, hc⟩ /
              algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨e, he⟩)) ∧
    ∃ Ψ : AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials ℂ K →ₗ[ℂ] (UpperHalfPlane → ℂ),
      Function.Injective Ψ ∧
      (∀ ω, MDifferentiable 𝓘(ℂ) 𝓘(ℂ) (Ψ ω)) ∧
      ∀ (ω : AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials ℂ K) (a b c e : UpperHalfPlane → ℂ)
        (ha : a ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) (hb : b ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N)
        (hc : c ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) (he : e ∈ ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N),
        b ≠ 0 → e ≠ 0 →
        (ω : KaehlerDifferential ℂ K) =
          (algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨a, ha⟩ /
              algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨b, hb⟩) •
            KaehlerDifferential.D ℂ K (algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨c, hc⟩ /
              algebraMap (ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N) K ⟨e, he⟩) →
        ∀ τ : UpperHalfPlane, Ψ ω τ * b τ * e τ ^ 2 =
          a τ * (e τ * deriv (c ∘ UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex) τ -
            c τ * deriv (e ∘ UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex) τ) := by sorry
